# Generated and downloaded data. None of it belongs in the repository: the FASTA files are
# reproduced by the goal `extractrefseqcsv' from the project's configuration, and everything under
# data/common is downloaded from the NCBI. Both run to tens of thousands of files and many
# gigabytes, and both are derived from what *is* tracked -- the taxids, categories and config files
# of each project.

# Per-accession FASTA files written by `extractrefseqcsv' (through the goal extractrefseqfasta).
/data/projects/*/fasta/

# Simulated and downloaded reads, together with the fastq mapping files that make_fastqs.sh writes
# next to them. Those maps are generated from the reads they point at and hold absolute paths, so
# they are valid only on the machine that produced them.
/data/fastq/*
# The accession list of the real Nanopore tick runs is input, not generated.
!/data/fastq/seventicks.txt
# So is the map that declares those runs by URL for the goal `fastqdownload'. It holds URLs rather
# than absolute paths, so unlike the generated maps above it is valid on any machine.
!/data/fastq/ticks_real.txt
# ... and the same for the human saliva runs the first paper used.
!/data/fastq/saliva_real.txt
# Single-sample maps, written by hand to score one file at a time. Like the two above they name
# files rather than absolute paths, so they are valid anywhere.
!/data/fastq/ticks_sim_tick1.txt
!/data/fastq/saliva_mate1.txt
!/data/fastq/saliva_srr5571991.txt
# The C. difficile isolates of PRJNA1148956, keyed by the source study's own isolate identifiers.
# Written by hand rather than generated: bin/fetch_cdiff.sh only downloads the files it names, and
# the mapping from an isolate to its runs is what the study's sequence types are joined through.
!/data/fastq/cdiff_isolates.txt
# ... and the sequence type of every isolate in that map, read off Table 2 of the source study.
# Input as much as the map is, and the ground truth the classification experiment is scored against:
# nothing regenerates it, so left out of the repository it is simply gone.
!/data/fastq/cdiff_isolates.txt.st.csv

# RefSeq and Genbank archives, the taxonomy dumps and the assembly summaries.
/data/common/*
# Re-include the directory itself before excluding its contents, since git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
!/data/common/fasta/
/data/common/fasta/*
# The list of extra genomes to download is project setup, not downloaded data.
!/data/common/fasta/downloads.txt

# Everything a project produces. Only its four configuration files -- taxids.txt, categories.txt,
# additional.txt and config.properties -- are input and belong in the repository; the rest is
# rebuilt from them by Genestrip's goals and runs to many gigabytes.
/data/projects/*/db/
/data/projects/*/csv/
/data/projects/*/fastq/
/data/projects/*/txt/
/data/projects/*/tex/
/data/projects/*/log/
/data/projects/*/krakenout/

# Experiment output. `run_exps.sh' and the classification runs write here, and the files are copied
# from here into the paper's own results folder, which is where the version that the paper builds
# from lives. Regenerating them means re-running the experiments, so keep a copy with the paper
# rather than relying on this directory.
/results/

# Tools installed by install_tools.sh, and Maven's build output. Both are reproducible.
/tools/
/target/

# Crash and scratch files that land in the project root.
hs_err_pid*.log
texput.log

# Editor and platform noise.
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.versionsBackup
